# Read by direnv when you enter the directory, and by nothing else.
#
# It loads the flake's devShell, which is the system half of the build:
# pkg-config, PipeWire's headers, and the C++ runtime that the onnxruntime in
# dist/linux/lib needs. Not the toolchain -- zig, bun and shellcheck come from
# mise, pinned in .mise.toml, so a local build uses the versions CI uses.
# mise puts those on PATH through its own shell hook; the two do not overlap.
#
# Guarded because this file is checked in and most contributors have no nix:
# for them direnv does nothing here and `./run` installs the same packages
# with apt or brew. Installing nix-direnv is worth it if you have nix --
# plain direnv re-evaluates the flake on every entry, where nix-direnv caches
# the result and roots it against the garbage collector.
if has nix; then
  use flake
fi
